      summary:
        '<p>Millions of Americans face air quality alerts from Minnesota to New York as authorities urge people to stay indoors</p><ul><li><p><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/feb/17/sign-up-for-the-breaking-news-us-email-to-get-newsletter-alerts-direct-to-your-inbox?utm_medium=ACQUISITIONS_STANDFIRST&amp;utm_campaign=BN22326&amp;utm_content=signup&amp;utm_term=standfirst&amp;utm_source=GUARDIAN_WEB">Sign up for the Breaking News US newsletter email</a><em> </em></p></li></ul><p>Smoke from wildfires burning in south-central <a href="https://apnews.com/article/wildfires-smoke-canada-minnesota-08d3fb58a434a5d42803ab1c2bbda0b3">Canada and parts of Minnesota</a> is spreading across the US, prompting air quality alerts in more than 20 states with millions of Americans expected to face unhealthy air conditions this week.</p><p>The smoke from the more than <a href="https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/ontario-wildfire-smoke-moves-east/">180</a> active <a href="https://www.theg',
