      summary:
        '<p>FDA notice warns of ‘potential foreign material’ as recall covers two types of frozen bread roll dough</p><p>General Mills is recalling nearly 736,000 Pillsbury bread rolls over concerns they could contain glass, according to a <a href="https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/ires/index.cfm?Product=221250">notice</a> issued by the US Food and Drug Administration earlier this week.</p><p>The recall covers two frozen bread roll products: 3,080 cases of Hard Roll Dough, with 180 rolls in each case, totaling 554,400 rolls, and 1,260 cases of Kaiser Roll Dough, with 144 rolls per case, totaling 181,440 rolls. The FDA notice states the products may contain “potential foreign material (glass)”.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/jul/16/pillsbury-general-mills-frozen-bread-rolls-recall">Continue reading...</a>',
